'''Siyaad Yussuf''' ({{IPA|so|siˈjaːd ˈjusːuf}}; born 8 December 1987) is an [[Balisca|Baliscan]] activist and politician serving as the [[Commissar of the Castejón Metropolis|Commissar for the Castejón Metropolis]] since 2024, and the incumbent delegate for [[Llanito]]'s third [[commune district]] since 2016. His public profile and popularity rapidly grew during his participation in the [[2021 Baliscan civil unrest|2021 protests in the Castejón Metropolis and surrounding areas]]. Upon taking office on 6 December, Yussuf simultaneously became the first {{W|Muslim}}, the [[Burawi Baliscans|first Burawi Baliscan]], and the youngest Metropolitan Commissar (37 years old) in Castejón's history. Yussuf has been noted for his substantial social media presence relative to his fellow members of the [[MetCo]]. 

Born to [[Burawa|Burawi immigrants]] in [[Llanito|Llanito's]] working class [[Andújar, Llanito|Andújar barrio]], Yussuf went on to attend [[Concordia University]], where he gained his degree in {{W|Bachelor of Architecture|Architecture}}. After university, he partook in several architectural ventures, before becoming an activist and running for election to the MetCo in 2016.

